.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn BN_bn2bin
converts the absolute value of
.Fa a
into big-endian form and stores it at
.Fa to .
.Fa to
must point to
.Pf BN_num_bytes( Fa a )
bytes of memory.
.Fa a
and
.Fa to
.Sy MUST NOT
be NULL.
.Pp
.Fn BN_bn2binpad
also converts the absolute value of
.Fa a
into big-endian form and stores it at
.Fa to .
.Fa tolen
indicates the length of the output buffer
.Fa to .
The result is padded with zeros if necessary.
If
.Fa tolen
is less than
.Pf BN_num_bytes( Fa a )
an error is returned.
.Pp
.Fn BN_signed_bn2bin
converts the value of
.Fa a
into big-endian signed 2's complements form and stores it at
.Fa to .
.Fa tolen
indicates the length of the output buffer
.Fa to .
The result is signed extended (padded with 0x00 for positive numbers or
with 0xff for negative numbers) if necessary.
If
.Fa tolen
is smaller than the necessary size (which may be
.Qo Li <BN_num_bytes( Ns Fa a Ns ) + 1 Qc Ns >),
an error is returned.
.Pp
.Fn BN_bin2bn
converts the positive integer in big-endian form of length
.Fa len
at
.Fa s
into a
.Vt BIGNUM
and places it in
.Fa ret .
If
.Fa ret
is NULL, a new
.Vt BIGNUM
is created.
.Fa s
.Sy MUST NOT
be NULL.
.Pp
.Fn BN_signed_bin2bn
converts the integer in big-endian signed 2's complement form of length
.Fa len
at
.Fa s
into a
.Vt BIGNUM
and places it in
.Fa ret .
If
.Fa ret
is NULL, a new
.Vt BIGNUM
is created.
.Pp
.Fn BN_bn2lebinpad ,
.Fn BN_signed_bn2lebin
and
.Fn BN_lebin2bn
are identical to
.Fn BN_bn2binpad ,
.Fn BN_signed_bn2bin
and
.Fn BN_bin2bn
except the buffer is in little-endian format.
.Pp
.Fn BN_bn2nativepad ,
.Fn BN_signed_bn2native
and
.Fn BN_native2bn
are identical to
.Fn BN_bn2binpad ,
.Fn BN_signed_bn2bin
and
.Fn BN_bin2bn
except the buffer is in native format, i.e.
most significant byte first on big-endian platforms, and least
significant byte first on little-endian platforms.
.Pp
.Fn BN_bn2hex
and
.Fn BN_bn2dec
return printable strings containing the hexadecimal and decimal encoding
of
.Fa a
respectively.
For negative numbers, the string is prefaced with a leading '-'. The
string must be freed later using
.Xr OPENSSL_free 3 .
.Pp
.Fn BN_hex2bn
takes as many characters as possible from the string
.Fa str ,
including the leading character '-' which means negative, to form a
valid hexadecimal number representation and converts them to a
.Vt BIGNUM
and stores it in
.Pf ** Fa a .
If
.Pf * Fa a
is NULL, a new
.Vt BIGNUM
is created.
If
.Fa a
is NULL, it only computes the length of valid representation.
A "negative zero" is converted to zero.
.Fn BN_dec2bn
is the same using the decimal system.
.Pp
.Fn BN_print
and
.Fn BN_print_fp
write the hexadecimal encoding of
.Fa a ,
with a leading '-' for negative numbers, to the
.Vt BIO
or
.Vt FILE
.Fa fp .
.Pp
.Fn BN_bn2mpi
and
.Fn BN_mpi2bn
convert
.Vt BIGNUM Ns s
from and to a format that consists of the number's length in bytes
represented as a 4-byte big-endian number, and the number itself in
big-endian format, where the most significant bit signals a negative
number (the representation of numbers with the MSB set is prefixed with
null byte).
.Pp
.Fn BN_bn2mpi
stores the representation of
.Fa a
at
.Fa to ,
where
.Fa to
must be large enough to hold the result.
The size can be determined by calling
.Pf BN_bn2mpi( Fa a ,
NULL).
.Pp
.Fn BN_mpi2bn
converts the
.Fa len
bytes long representation at
.Fa s
to a
.Vt BIGNUM
and stores it at
.Fa ret ,
or in a newly allocated
.Vt BIGNUM
if
.Fa ret
is NULL.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn BN_bn2bin
returns the length of the big-endian number placed at
.Fa to .
.Fn BN_bin2bn
returns the
.Vt BIGNUM ,
NULL on error.
.Pp
.Fn BN_bn2binpad ,
.Fn BN_signed_bn2bin ,
.Fn BN_bn2lebinpad ,
.Fn BN_signed_bn2lebin ,
.Fn BN_bn2nativepad ,
and_signed
.Xr BN_bn2native 3
return the number of bytes written or -1 if the supplied buffer is too
small.
.Pp
.Fn BN_bn2hex
and
.Fn BN_bn2dec
return a NUL-terminated string, or NULL on error.
.Fn BN_hex2bn
and
.Fn BN_dec2bn
return the number of characters used in parsing, or 0 on error, in which
case no new
.Vt BIGNUM
will be created.
.Pp
.Fn BN_print_fp
and
.Fn BN_print
return 1 on success, 0 on write errors.
.Pp
.Fn BN_bn2mpi
returns the length of the representation.
.Fn BN_mpi2bn
returns the
.Vt BIGNUM ,
and NULL on error.
.Pp
The error codes can be obtained by
.Xr ERR_get_error 3 .
